00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:04.960
Hi, I'm Alex Greer with the IBM Cloud team.&nbsp;
Today I want to talk aboutIBM Cloud Secrets&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:08.560
Manager. But, before I get into it, don't&nbsp;
forget to hit that "Subscribe" button!&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:14.880
As enterprises build more microservices and become&nbsp;
globally distributed, securing your application&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:20.400
secret data becomes much more complex. As we saw&nbsp;
before in my previous video, secrets management&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:25.360
services enable the secure management of digital&nbsp;
credentials that ultimately allow entities&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.360 --> 00:00:31.520
to securely interact with services.IBM Cloud&nbsp;
Secrets Manager is a service based on open-source&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.520 --> 00:00:37.680
HashiCorp Vault designed to securely manage&nbsp;
the lifecycle of Secrets, such as IAM API Keys,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:44.560
User credentials, or different forms of arbitrary&nbsp;
text.&nbsp;This allows IT security leaders to dream big&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.560 --> 00:00:48.960
about their cloud native application future&nbsp;
without being concerned about data breaches&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:54.160
from mismanaged credentials, or losing velocity in&nbsp;
their developer operations while securing secrets.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.960 --> 00:01:00.560
Secrets Manager centralizes the experience&nbsp;
of&nbsp;generating, storing, rotating, and revoking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:05.920
multiple types of secrets from a single pane&nbsp;
of glass. Integrations with other services such&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.920 --> 00:01:11.600
as your private catalogs in IBM Cloud enables&nbsp;
the retrieval of your secrets in-context when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.600 --> 00:01:16.640
you need them, streamlining your workflows.&nbsp;&nbsp;
Through leasing, it even allows for you to give&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.640 --> 00:01:21.520
an application or a team member temporary access&nbsp;
to a service to complete their respective task.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.240 --> 00:01:28.000
As a managed service, Secrets Manager offers much&nbsp;
of the same benefit of an on-premise deployment of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:33.520
Vault without the hassle of having to maintain its&nbsp;
tricky operators, or manage and ultimately operate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.520 --> 00:01:38.720
its underlying infrastructure. This allows you&nbsp;
to keep your desired security posture at scale,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.280 --> 00:01:45.440
while we take care of the rest.&nbsp;A critical element&nbsp;
of Secrets Manager that makes it’s so powerful&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.440 --> 00:01:50.400
is its unique trust model. Built for enterprises&nbsp;
that have very little tolerance for any sort of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:55.680
data vulnerabilities but need the velocity&nbsp;
provided by the cloud.&nbsp; This model starts by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.680 --> 00:02:00.960
allowing you to seal your vault and encrypt all of&nbsp;
your hosted secrets with your own root encryption&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:07.680
key.&nbsp;For example — one of your existing&nbsp;
FIPS compliant keys from IBM Key Protect,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.240 --> 00:02:15.280
giving you ownership of your data. Next, your data&nbsp;
is protected in transit through TLS — Your vault&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.280 --> 00:02:21.520
as well as the UI and APIs you use to interact&nbsp;
with it are all single-tenant. Meaning, your&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.520 --> 00:02:28.320
data is isolated in your own dedicated silo and&nbsp;
doesn’t rely on any shared components. And…should&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.320 --> 00:02:33.360
you decide to delete your instance you have the&nbsp;
peace of mind that your data is cryptographically&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:38.560
deleted. Thanks for listening to this introduction&nbsp;
of IBM Cloud Secrets Manager. To get started&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.560 --> 00:02:49.840
with improving the security of your secrets&nbsp;
come check us out in the IBM Cloud catalog.

